#{[17592186369278 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369278 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369278 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9230ca12-f5f1-5580-9077-a7bbc7def856" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387470 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387470 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387470 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/47/4727c988042bd8d63af370c507db8988b3024cf7e75c86d40bc70cdcfd744873.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}y{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a circle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76ca20f1-204f-59f9-8369-ed13b85fecd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387470 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot {e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot {e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186387473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387471 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1a48ec71-cabe-53f3-8125-9985126072d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387472 #edb/ref 1080 "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387472 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387472 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "66dc688f-81a1-5bab-892b-ab84541785d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387473 #edb/ref 1080 "-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387473 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387473 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d1cf7a39-05f3-5b46-9687-4304489da63d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387474 #edb/ref 1080 "-2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387474 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387474 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3aaa33f-356e-5b31-9322-7fc460783b0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387475 #edb/ref 1080 "-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387475 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387475 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6904468a-7356-52cb-8fc4-603b5ee7fd3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387476 #edb/ref 1080 "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387476 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387476 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3bac43c-45b2-592b-a306-006e20a13c19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387491 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124293" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387491 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387491 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/4d/4d02a56e1f927ccf8bd76a6fcc46dec61259649176695912865dd050657ce7f0.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along a quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4,$ traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387491 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e84b6989-0b06-5564-bfd3-0660ddb2a037" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387491 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186387495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387492 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1af7ee7b-5d10-5025-8624-92a4d018ecb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387493 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387493 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387493 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2cc88e3d-a852-5587-8a01-ed034f9f4385" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387494 #edb/ref 1080 "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387494 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387494 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0354e92a-880d-5b37-9463-ad3a8ea451ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387495 #edb/ref 1080 "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387495 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387495 #edb/re